infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Parallel DB isolation: cost climbs as fidelity climbs
  desc Per-test setup cost — take the cheapest rung that still exercises what you assert
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Txn-per-test rollback · ~1–3 ms
      desc Fastest and leak-free, but writes never commit — can't test commit-triggered triggers, deferred constraints, or multi-connection visibility.
    - label Schema/DB per worker · ~tens of ms
      desc TRUNCATE tables between tests; slower than rollback but exercises real commits, with each worker fully isolated.
    - label Ephemeral container · ~seconds
      desc Maximum fidelity — exact engine version and real extensions — so costly you run far fewer and amortize across many tests.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
